{"step_index":94,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-10T12:43:47Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-10T15:43:47+03:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-10T15:43:47+03:00\nCommand exited with code 0.\n\nCommand output:\ncannot re-enable capture after mute/Leave. For host-owned meetings, the helper watches the host heartbeat\r\nand ends media if ownership is lost; host failure cleanup targets only its own\r\nlaunched process and does not automatically fall back to a second SDK session.\r\n\r\n## Validation\r\n\r\nDeterministic checks:\r\n\r\n```sh\r\nbash Experiments/NativeGuestTests/run-session.sh\r\nbash Experiments/NativeGuestTests/run-engine.sh\r\nbash Experiments/NativeGuestTests/run-companion-policy.sh\r\nbash NativeMacGuest/test-standalone.sh\r\nbash NativeMacGuest/test-rock.sh \\\r\n  --framework-root .build/webrtc-m156-desktop-audio/native-framework-r4\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe Rock adapter unit harness defaults to the current r4 framework. It prepares\r\nits pinned LiveKit source and compiler outputs under\r\n`.build/native-rock-unit/<framework SHA256>/`, verifies that the built SDK uses\r\nthat exact WebRTC binary, then runs synthetic bridge, policy and lifecycle\r\nchecks. It does not join a room or start physical capture. Older framework\r\nexperiments remain available by passing another `--framework-root`; their\r\ncompiler outputs are isolated by binary identity. Optional `--dependency-dir`,\r\n`--sdk-build-dir` and `--sdk-source` override those paths explicitly. The generic\r\n`prepare-livekit.py` defaults remain unchanged for existing experiments.\r\n\r\nThe standalone harness uses the real meeting controller with a fake media\r\nengine, waits beyond the host-death timeout, verifies media-off join/Leave/rejoin,\r\nblocks rejoin after failed teardown, and exercises exact-PID, one-use host-ticket\r\nadmission. It does not qualify a live provider or physical media.\r\n#!/bin/bash\r\nset -euo pipefail\r\nsource_dir=\"$(cd -- \"$(dirname -- \"$0\")\" && pwd)\"\r\nrepo_dir=\"$(dirname -- \"$source_dir\")\"\r\nframework_root=\"${NATIVE_GUEST_FRAMEWORK_ROOT:-$repo_dir/.build/webrtc-m156-desktop-audio/native-framework-r4}\"\r\ndependency_root=\"${NATIVE_GUEST_LIVEKIT_DEPENDENCIES:-}\"\r\nlivekit_\n<truncated 1125 bytes>\nnfo['AvailableLibraries'] if value['SupportedPlatform'] == 'macos' and 'arm64' in value['SupportedArchitectures']]\r\nif len(slices) != 1: raise SystemExit('Expected exactly one native arm64 macOS framework slice')\r\nbinary = framework / slices[0]['LibraryIdentifier'] / slices[0]['LibraryPath'] / 'LiveKitWebRTC'\r\ndigest = hashlib.sha256()\r\nwith binary.open('rb') as stream:\r\n    for chunk in iter(lambda: stream.read(1024 * 1024), b''): digest.update(chunk)\r\nprint(digest.hexdigest())\r\nPYFRAMEWORK\r\n)\"\r\n# The binary identity isolates both source/package state and compiler outputs.\r\n# Selecting an older artifact never repoints the baseline SDK or its framework.\r\nunit_root=\"$repo_dir/.build/native-rock-unit/$framework_sha\"\r\ndependency_root=\"${dependency_root:-$unit_root/Dependencies}\"\r\nlivekit_dir=\"${livekit_dir:-$unit_root/LiveKitDerived}\"\r\nbuild_dir=\"$(mktemp -d \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/native-guest-rock.XXXXXX\")\"\r\ntrap 'rm -rf -- \"$build_dir\"' EXIT\r\npython3 \"$source_dir/prepare-livekit.py\" --source \"$sdk_source\" \\\r\n    --framework \"$framework_root/LiveKitWebRTC.xcframework\" --destination \"$dependency_root\"\r\nlivekit_source=\"$dependency_root/client-sdk-swift\"\r\ncore_dir=\"${NATIVE_GUEST_CORE_BUILD_DIR:-$repo_dir/.build/native-guest/library-core}\"\r\nswift build --package-path \"$livekit_source\" --scratch-path \"$livekit_dir\" --product LiveKit\r\nswift build --package-path \"$repo_dir/ConferenceCore\" --scratch-path \"$core_dir\" --product ConferenceCore\r\nproducts=\"$(swift build --package-path \"$livekit_source\" --scratch-path \"$livekit_dir\" --show-bin-path)\"\r\ncore_products=\"$(swift build --package-path \"$repo_dir/ConferenceCore\" --scratch-path \"$core_dir\" --show-bin-path)\"\r\npython3 - \"$dependency_root/native-livekit.json\" \"$products/LiveKitWebRTC.framework/LiveKitWebRTC\" <<'PYVERIFY'\r\nimport hashlib, json, pathlib, sys\r\nmarker = json.loads(pathlib.Path(sys.argv[1]).read_text())\r\ndigest = hashlib.sha256()\r\nwith pathlib.Path(sys.argv[2]).open('rb') as stream:\r\n    for chunk in iter(lambda: stream.read(1024 * 1024), b''): digest.update(chunk)\r\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
