{"step_index":136,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-10T12:49:58Z","input_tokens":2313,"cache_read_tokens":83981,"output_tokens":556,"content":"Both changes are implemented and all 17 tests in [`SharedAudioEngineTests`](file:///Users/v.smirnov/docs/conference-guest-ios/NativeMacGuest/Tests/Parity/SharedAudioEngineTests.swift) pass:\n\n1. **Skip redundant native mute during engine rebuilds** ([`SharedAudioEngine.swift`](file:///Users/v.smirnov/docs/conference-guest-ios/NativeMacGuest/Engines/SharedAudioEngine.swift#L89-L92), [`engineChanged(_:)`](file:///Users/v.smirnov/docs/conference-guest-ios/NativeMacGuest/Engines/SharedAudioEngine.swift#L336-L348)):\n   - Tracks `muteConfirmed` whenever a native `setMicrophoneMuted(true)` succeeds and resets it before any unmute attempt, private check, failed mute, or module teardown.\n   - When `engineChanged(.stopped)` fires while `muteConfirmed && moduleMuted && !talkUnmuted && !privateCheckActive`, senders are still disabled immediately, but the redundant blocking `setMicrophoneMuted(true)` call into the rebuilding ADM worker (and the follow-up `suppressMicrophone()` after timeout) is skipped.\n   - Added [`testRebuildWhileConfirmedMutedSkipsTheNativeMute`](file:///Users/v.smirnov/docs/conference-guest-ios/NativeMacGuest/Tests/Parity/SharedAudioEngineTests.swift#L254-L273) covering both confirmed-muted skips and unconfirmed-mute fallback.\n\n2. **Per-event audio engine lifecycle & route logging** ([`GuestSystemAudio.swift`](file:///Users/v.smirnov/docs/conference-guest-ios/Experiments/NativeGuest/GuestSystemAudio.swift#L361-L382)):\n   - Logs `audio-engine-lifecycle` (`engine-created`, `engine-start`, `engine-stop`, `engine-released`, `device-update`) with all lifecycle counters, whether an owner operation was active (`ownOperation`), and active operation summary from [`GuestAudioOperationTrace.activeSummary()`](file:///Users/v.smirnov/docs/conference-guest-ios/Experiments/NativeGuest/GuestSystemAudio.swift#L313-L320).\n   - On `device-update`, dispatches an off-worker `GuestAcousticEnvironment.boundedRoute(timeout: 1)` read and logs `audio-device-route` so future diagnostics bundles show the exact sequence of CoreAudio route updates and engine rebuilds."}
